nce they were infants when  they lived on level zero now as Sophia  and Vivian are 16 years old and live on  level 16. they start to question their  strange lives it's up to Sophia and  Vivian to learn the true nature of their  school and their very existence if they  want to escape film writer Richard  Krause commented on the film saying  mixing elements of social justice horror  and sci-fi level 16 is a genre movie  that delivers both intellectually and  emotionally a little bit of a bullet  riddled crime caper as well as a little  bit of a romantic comedy the Abundant  charm in Mr Right lies in where those  two diametrically opposed film schools  Collide Sam Rockwell plays much in aloof  morally flexible xci agent who spends  his days as a reactive assassin always  working on killing those who've been  hired to kill him but then he meets a  lonely young woman named Martha Sparks  immediately fly and these two fragile  people begin a sweet romance even after  Martha finds out about Munch's violent  world of intrigue she even comes to  enjoy the dangerous excitement a  relationship can offer despite putting  herself In Harm's Way Devin Coggin of  Entertainment Weekly writes the unlikely  Duo of Kendrick and Rockwell make this  candy colored Carnival of blood and  romance hard to resist gosh you're cute  likewise Andy Webster of the New York  Times enjoyed the quote screwball  efferves of Mr Right  a monster calls sounds like the name of  a horror movie but it's actually a  spielberg-esque tale of Boyhood fantasy  director J.A bayona crafts an  allegorical eye-popping film about all  too real and difficult emotions from the  point of view of a child which makes it  all the more heartbreaking yes a monster  calls is about grief but it's also about  a walking talking tree creature with the  voice of Liam Neeson Conor is 13 and his  mother is dying he's just old enough to  know what's going on but young enough to  have no idea how to cope he can't turn  to his Stern gr