ion design and the men's own fear  and misjudgment to create the sense of  pervasive Doom not much sleep happens in  the sleepover it's a heist movie and a  kidnapping paper with a Switcheroo in  that it's the kids who need to save the  grown-ups it's one of those movies where  tweens get to stay up all night and go  on a Grand Adventure goofy mother Margot  was once an international Master Thief  who quit that life entered witness  protection and married her dweebie  husband Ron the past comes back to haunt  her when her old team recruits her by  way of kidnapping her and Ron and forces  her to help them steal a precious Crown  from a dignitary your mom is getting  cooler by like the second when Margot  and Ron's kids come home to an empty  house they figure out their mother's  secret life and potential whereabouts  and set out to rescue her with the aid  of criminal and spy gadgetry she left  behind small crimes is a small crime  movie about people on the fringes of  society who have seemingly resigned  themselves to life on the edge it's an  it's an addling take on the crime drama  genre Nikolai Koster wildau plays a  fallen from Grace police officer just  emerging from prison after serving six  years for attempted murder he wants to  get his life on track and redeem himself  with his family but they don't want much  to do with him this helps to send him  headlong back into a world of corruption  organized crime casual violence and  other CD elements Mike D'Angelo of the  AV club said if the film came across as  jaded and cynical it might well be hard  to take instead it seems weary and  defeated as if some people are simply  born to fail with the Waterman David  oyalo both takes a supporting role as a  put upon father and directs this  dazzling family-friendly fantasy drama  about the power of a child's imagination  it's an Escapist movie about the  pleasures and necessities of escapism  the Boone family has just moved to a  Tiny Town in Rural Oregon where  eleven-year-old Gunner finds Alice in  the local bookstore and it's here that  he researches detective stories and  cancer because his mother is coping with  leukemia Gunner needs breaks from  reality and he finds one when he hears  about the watermen a mythical figure who  factors large in local Legend So Gunner  pays a local nerdu well to take him deep  into the woods to see if they can find  this ghostly individual who may possibly  be real and who may possibly be immortal  their Quest winds up equal parts surreal  magical and mysterious Adam Graham of  the Detroit News commands oyelowo for  his storytelling and big imagination and  describes the film saying it's a  sensitive coming-of-age story about loss  friendship and the need to believe in  magic  with his headlining role in the twisty  harrowing 2018 action thriller the  wedding guest Dev Patel proves he's one  of the most versatile and captivating  actors working in movies right now Patel  plays Jay a British man with criminal  ties hired to travel to Pakistan and  violently kidnap a woman named Samira  from her own wedding he's methodical  careful and cold-blooded and yet what's  supposed to be a simple and horrific  task completely falls apart innocent  bystanders get victimized Ransom  payments go awry and both the failed  kidnapper and the ill-fated bride to be  are harboring some pretty major Secrets  simran Hans of The Observer said that  the film pays homage to the quote Neo  Noir genre while MV Moorhead of Phoenix  magazine said the story feels realistic  in a way that this sort of Noir material  doesn't always what lies below begins  innocently enough Liberty Wells is a  quiet slightly awkward teen who's just  finishing up a spell at summer camp when  she heads back to meet her mother at an  idyllic Lake house but Mom Michelle has  some news she's got a new boyfriend and  he's at the lake house too at first the  only thing that seems truly off about  the hunky John Smith is his mysteriously  generic name but as Liberty gets to know  him he emerges as a truly and alarmingly  weird guy he hangs out at the lake all  year engaging in some kind of  cryptically explained research about  various species he can also Sleepwalk  into a lake into a glowing light under  the water and come out totally dry his  oddness grows ever the more Sinister and  life-threatening her mother can't see  that John Smith is dangerous and it's up  to the teenager to unravel and expose  what's really going on before someone  ends up dead Drew tinnin of dread  Central says the film really works as a  sexy sci-fi thriller that definitely has  a will to be weird so if you're in the  mood for some creepy science fiction  head over to Netflix to find out what  truly does lie below very awesome thanks  generally speaking westerns are often  filled with stock characters Cowboys and  can-do settlers who meet every challenge  with style but the reality of life in  the old west must have been objectively  terrifying at times and this is the  theme explored by director Emma Tami in  the 2018 Western psychological horror  movie The Wind in the 1800s Lizzie  Macklin settles on a lonely patch of  land out on the frontier where she's cut  off from civilization and most of  humanity for long periods of time she  faces Relentless challenges particularly  the endlessly howling wind that starts  to play tricks on her mind in fact she's  starting to believe that there's  something evil and Sinister afoot  forcing her to resort to Desperate  Measures Audrey Fox of crooked Marquis  said the wind is a piece of surprisingly  intimate female-oriented historical  horror there are no jump scares it opts  instead for a tense pervasive sense of  dread that permeates the entire film  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more Looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the Bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

